{"created": "2026-11-14T17:57:56.412379+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-18T20:14:51.050516+00:00", "id": 24225551, "conceptrecid": "24225550", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24225551", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24225550", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24225551", "metadata": {"title": "Assistive Technology Microdata in the Brazilian Unified Health System (SUS) \u2014 2022\u20132024 Triennium: Audited National Census Database Linked to the 2022 IBGE Demographic Census", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24225551", "publication_date": "2026-11-14", "description": "<p>Nationwide, audited census dataset on the provision of Assistive Technology (AT) within the Brazilian Unified Health System (SUS) during the post-pandemic triennium (2022&ndash;2024).&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The dataset was constructed from an exhaustive scan of 1,779,894,079 raw outpatient records from the Outpatient Information System (SIA/SUS, PA files), covering 100% of Brazil's 5,570 municipalities across 972 state-month partitions in columnar Apache Parquet format. Clinical and forensic curation of the SIGTAP official health classification audited 226 procedures, retaining 167 strict AT procedures (131 physical device provisions and 36 clinical rehabilitation and fitting acts) and excluding 59 non-rehabilitation items.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The finalized database contains 2,089,337 approved billings totaling BRL 1,270,170,973.83 reimbursed by the public health system (2,167,191 physical devices delivered and 330,358 clinical acts), deterministically linked to the 14.4 million persons with disabilities identified in the 2022 IBGE National Demographic Census and to 592 healthcare facilities registered in the National Registry of Health Establishments (CNES, Dec/2024).</p>\n<p>Funding: Research Program for the SUS: Shared Health Management (PPSUS) &mdash; Ministry of Health of Brazil (Decit/SECTICS), National Council for Scientific and Technological Development (CNPq), Carlos Chagas Filho Foundation for Research Support of the State of Rio de Janeiro (FAPERJ), and Foundation for Research Support of the State of Amazonas (FAPEAM). Interinstitutional partnership between the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro (UFRJ) and the Federal University of Amazonas (UFAM).</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Rodrigues, Hidelbrando Ferreira", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal do Amazonas", "orcid": "0000-0003-1266-0957"}, {"name": "Alonso, Carolina", "affiliation": "Universidade Federal do Rio de Janeiro Faculdade de Medicina", "orcid": "0000-0003-4928-4465"}], "keywords": ["Assistive Technology", "Unified Health System (SUS)", "Persons with Disabilities", "Rehabilitation"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24225550"}}]}}, "title": "Assistive Technology Microdata in the Brazilian Unified Health System (SUS) \u2014 2022\u20132024 Triennium: Audited National Census Database Linked to the 2022 IBGE Demographic Census", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24225551", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24225551", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24225551?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24225551", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24225551", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24225551", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24225551/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24225550", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24225550", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24225550", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24225550", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24225551/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24225551/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24225551/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/